  "agent": {
    "qa-generator": {
      "description": "Generates Playwright E2E tests for a commit's blast radius and writes them in e2e/. Has serena+engram+playwright MCP access by design (test author), except the memory-conflict tools (judge, compare), because resolving a conflict between memories is not the generator's job, mem_session_summary, because the generator ends on its verdict and has no session to summarize, and the tools that run code, push a file or open a shell (browser_run_code_unsafe, browser_evaluate, browser_file_upload, browser_drop, execute_shell_command). It has no shell at all (permission.bash is denied outright, for every target): the orchestrator's Validate and Execute phases compile, lint, list and run what it writes. Enforced here: no shell, no code-running or file-pushing browser tool. Not enforced: browser_click, browser_type and browser_fill_form can still submit a form on DEV through the UI, which only the prompt forbids (live DEV is observed while authoring; a generated spec is what writes to it). It also holds the authbrowser_* tools, served by the orchestrator: a read-only browser signed in as the test account, whose session the agent never holds; the orchestrator refuses them unless the run granted them.",
      "mode": "primary",
      "model": "opencode-go/glm-5.3-flash",
      "prompt": "{file:./agent/qa-generator.md}",
      "tools": {
        "write": true,
        "edit": true,
        "read": true,
        "run_spec": true,
        "authbrowser_navigate": true,
        "authbrowser_snapshot": true,
