    "qa-sidekick": {
      "description": "Coordination sidekick — a bounded delegation executor, invoked by the deterministic router for larger blast radii instead of the lead. Receives a self-contained delegation brief (objective, acceptance criteria, writable/readable scope, known facts, validation plan) and, unlike the single-spec-per-session parallel worker, may edit multiple EXISTING specs within its writable scope across follow-up feedback turns in the SAME session. Frozen authority: cannot change acceptance criteria/architecture, cannot write outside writablePaths, never performs git writes; a claimed result is externally validated against what actually exists on disk. Has serena + playwright MCP access by design (no engram — operational context only, never test-authoring rules), minus the tools that run code, push a file or open a shell (its built-in shell is off too). Enforced: those tools are denied. Not enforced: browser_click, browser_type and browser_fill_form can still submit a form on DEV through the UI, which only the prompt forbids. It also holds run_spec and the authbrowser_* tools, served by the orchestrator when the run granted them for the flow it is authoring (run_spec runs the one spec the flow was given, once, against DEV; the browser is a read-only one signed in as the test account); a session the run did not grant them hides them. It works in a workspace of its own, a copy of what the run may read, and the orchestrator takes back only the files its brief names.",
      "mode": "primary",
